<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>printing-methods</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="../css/cut-and-sew.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="../css/polos.css">
</head>

<body>
     <%- include('partials/nav') %>
    <section class="hero-section">
        <div class="hero-bg-container">
            <img src="../photos/printing-methods.webp" alt="Vito and Will folded polo shirts" class="hero-image">
        </div>

    </section>
    <section class="manufacturing-services">
        <div class="container">
            <h2 class="section-title">Custom Screen Printing Services</h2>

            <p class="section-text">
                At Wuzwear Industry, we specialize in all-over screen printing services backed by over two decades of
                experience. This expertise allows us to master every printing method, ensuring flawless results for your
                brand’s designs. From simple logos to highly creative and complex patterns, we bring your ideas to life
                with precision and durability.


            </p>

            <p class="section-text">
                We use advanced inks, updated machinery, and high-quality processes to ensure that every print maintains
                sharpness, consistency, and longevity. Whether you need unique pocket prints, sleeve logos, or full
                garment coverage, our team ensures your collection stands out from the competition.



            </p>
            <p>Wuzwear Industry provides multiple printing techniques to suit every design requirement, including silk
                screen printing, sublimation, heat transfer, digital printing, and direct-to-garment printing.

            </p>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="services-section">
        <div class="container">

            <div class="service-row">
                <div class="service-image">
                    <img src="../photos/printing-methods1.webp" alt="Close up of hands using a sewing machine">
                </div>
                <div class="service-content">
                    <h2 class="service-title">Silk Screen Printing</h2>
                    <p class="service-text">
                        Silk screen printing is one of the most popular and versatile methods for applying designs on
                        apparel such as t-shirts, hoodies, and jackets. Its fabric-friendly process allows for solid,
                        vibrant prints on a wide range of materials. At Wuzwear Industry, we use refined techniques to
                        produce sharp, accurate results—even for complex designs and placements.


                    </p>

                    <a href="#" class="trigger-popup-btn btn-quote">Get a Qoute</a>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="service-row row-reverse">
                <div class="service-image">
                    <img src="../photos/printing-methods2.webp" alt="Tailor working with denim fabric at a workbench">
                </div>
                <div class="service-content">
                    <h2 class="service-title">Flock Screen Printing</h2>
                    <p class="service-text">
                        Flock screen printing creates a velvety, textured finish by adding fine fibers to adhesive-based
                        prints. The result is a soft, raised effect that makes logos and graphics stand out, giving
                        garments a premium, tactile appeal.


                    </p>

                    <a href="#" class="trigger-popup-btn btn-quote">Get a Qoute</a>
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="dye-services-section">
        <div class="container">

            <div class="dye-row">
                <div class="dye-image">
                    <img src="../photos/printing-methods3.webp" alt="Colorful sublimated and dyed athletic t-shirts">
                </div>
                <div class="dye-content">
                    <h2 class="dye-title">Water-Based / Pigment Screen Printing
                    </h2>
                    <p class="dye-text">
                        This eco-friendly method uses water-based pigments to create soft and breathable prints. Best
                        suited for light-colored fabrics, it offers a smooth finish that blends seamlessly into the
                        fabric for a natural feel.


                    </p>
                    <a href="#" class="trigger-popup-btn btn-quote">Get a Qoute</a>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="dye-row row-reverse">
                <div class="dye-image">
                    <img src="../photos/printing-methods4.webp"
                        alt="A collection of vibrant fabric color swatches arranged together">
                </div>
                <div class="dye-content">
                    <h2 class="dye-title">Discharge Screen Printing</h2>
                    <p class="dye-text">
                        Discharge printing works by removing the garment’s original dye and replacing it with new
                        colors. This creates vibrant, soft-to-touch prints that feel like part of the fabric itself.
                        It’s a preferred technique for fashion-forward brands seeking high-quality finishes.


                    </p>
                    <a href="#" class="trigger-popup-btn btn-quote">Get a Qoute</a>
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="services-section">
        <div class="container">

            <div class="service-row">
                <div class="service-image">
                    <img src="../photos/printing-methods5.webp" alt="Close up of hands using a sewing machine">
                </div>
                <div class="service-content">
                    <h2 class="service-title">High-Density (3D) Printing</h2>
                    <p class="service-text">
                        By layering thick inks with high viscosity, high-density printing creates a bold, raised 3D
                        texture. Ideal for hoodies, jackets, and heavy fabrics, this technique adds depth and dimension
                        to designs, making them more eye-catching.



                    </p>

                    <a href="#" class="trigger-popup-btn btn-quote">Get a Qoute</a>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="service-row row-reverse">
                <div class="service-image">
                    <img src="../photos/printing-methods6.webp" alt="Tailor working with denim fabric at a workbench">
                </div>
                <div class="service-content">
                    <h2 class="service-title">Crack Screen Printing</h2>
                    <p class="service-text">
                        Also known as shatter printing, this technique produces unique cracked textures that add a
                        vintage or distressed look to garments. Each design has its own distinctive pattern, making
                        every piece one-of-a-kind.




                    </p>

                    <a href="#" class="trigger-popup-btn btn-quote">Get a Qoute</a>
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>
    </section>
       <section class="services-section">
        <div class="container">

            <div class="service-row">
                <div class="service-image">
                    <img src="../photos/printing-methods7.webp" alt="Close up of hands using a sewing machine">
                </div>
                <div class="service-content">
                    <h2 class="service-title">Puff Screen Printing</h2>
                    <p class="service-text">
                     Using heat-reactive inks, puff printing expands to create a raised, soft effect. It’s perfect for adding vintage charm or highlighting specific design elements on t-shirts, sweatshirts, and jackets.




                    </p>

                    <a href="#" class="trigger-popup-btn btn-quote">Get a Qoute</a>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="service-row row-reverse">
                <div class="service-image">
                    <img src="../photos/printing-methods8.webp" alt="Tailor working with denim fabric at a workbench">
                </div>
                <div class="service-content">
                    <h2 class="service-title">Glow-in-the-Dark Printing</h2>
                    <p class="service-text">
                        This specialty process uses neon inks that illuminate in low light, creating fun, bold designs. Ideal for themed collections, streetwear, or costumes, glow-in-the-dark prints work especially well on darker fabrics.




                    </p>

                    <a href="#" class="trigger-popup-btn btn-quote">Get a Qoute</a>
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>
    </section>
     <section class="dye-services-section">
        <div class="container">

            <div class="dye-row">
                <div class="dye-image">
                    <img src="..//photos/printing-methods9.webp" alt="Colorful sublimated and dyed athletic t-shirts">
                </div>
                <div class="dye-content">
                    <h2 class="dye-title">Dye Sublimation Printing

                    </h2>
                    <p class="dye-text">
                       Sublimation uses heat to transfer high-resolution designs directly into the fabric fibers, resulting in vibrant, fade-resistant prints. It’s ideal for all-over graphics and intricate artwork.



                    </p>
                    <a href="#" class="trigger-popup-btn btn-quote">Get a Qoute</a>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="dye-row row-reverse">
                <div class="dye-image">
                    <img src="../photos/printing-methods10.webp"
                        alt="A collection of vibrant fabric color swatches arranged together">
                </div>
                <div class="dye-content">
                    <h2 class="dye-title">Heat Transfer Printing</h2>
                    <p class="dye-text">
                       Heat transfer printing applies pre-printed designs onto fabric using heat and pressure. Often used for tagless labels and small details, it offers durability and clean finishes without cracking or peeling.




                    </p>
                    <a href="#" class="trigger-popup-btn btn-quote">Get a Qoute</a>
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>
    </section>
    <section>
        <div class="container">
            <div class="service-row">
                <div class="service-image">
                    <img src="../photos/printing-methods11.webp" alt="Close up of hands using a sewing machine">
                </div>
                <div class="service-content">
                    <h2 class="service-title">Digital Printing</h2>
                    <p class="service-text">
                        Digital printing is perfect for small batches and detailed designs, including photographic images. It allows for quick production with vibrant colors and long-lasting results, ideal for custom runs and limited editions.



                    </p>

                    <a href="#" class="trigger-popup-btn btn-quote">Get a Qoute</a>
                </div>
            </div>
    </section>

<%- include('partials/popup') %>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>

</body>

</html>
